# An optional number travels in a floating-point register, undefined as a bit pattern no number has. `value ?? 1` is one comparison of the bits. Null cannot come, so it is not asked for, and nothing is boxed or unboxed.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="orOne" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Double b@[[value]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[bits]] = BitwiseCast(b@[[value]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isUndefined]] = {{*}}b@[[bits]]{{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isUndefined]], Terminal
# CHECK: Double b@[[result]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[result]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
